## 1. The controller is switched off

| | |
|---|---|
| **What we do** | Power down the controller completely. |
| **What you should see** | Every light still switches on and off **from the wall switch**. |
| **Why it matters** | Automation is added on top of a working house, not in place of one. If a smart switch stops responding to the wall, that is a defect, not a limitation. |
| Result | ☐ Pass ☐ Fail |
| Notes | |

## 2. The internet connection is disconnected

| | |
|---|---|
| **What we do** | Unplug the internet feed at the gateway. |
| **What you should see** | Lights, thermostats, sensors, cameras and recording all continue to work. Automations continue to run. Only remote access from outside the house stops. |
| **Why it matters** | Nothing in your home depends on a company's cloud service staying online — including ours. |
| Result | ☐ Pass ☐ Fail |
| Notes | |

## 3. Power to the rack is cut

| | |
|---|---|
| **What we do** | Cut mains power to the equipment rack. |
| **What you should see** | The UPS takes over. You receive a notification. The system keeps recording. If power does not return, the system shuts down in an orderly way instead of dropping dead. |
{% if paquete_def.energia is defined and paquete_def.energia.ups_camaras_dedicado %}
| **Additional** | Cameras and recording continue on their dedicated battery for the designed runtime. |
{% endif %}
| **Why it matters** | Deliberate power interruption is the failure that actually matters for a camera system. |
| Result | ☐ Pass ☐ Fail |
| Notes | |

## 4. External port scan

| | |
|---|---|
| **What we do** | Scan your public address from outside your network. |
| **What you should see** | **No open ports.** The clean scan result is attached to this record. |
| **Why it matters** | No inbound exposure removes an entire class of attack. This is the only test that shows what an attacker actually sees. |
| Result | ☐ Pass ☐ Fail |
| Scan attached | ☐ Yes |

## 5. Remote access over cellular

| | |
|---|---|
| **What we do** | Turn Wi-Fi off on your phone, use the mobile network, open the app. |
| **What you should see** | The system responds. Live camera views load. |
| **Why it matters** | Testing from your home Wi-Fi proves nothing. This is the test that shows the encrypted tunnel works. |
| Result | ☐ Pass ☐ Fail |
| Notes | |

## 6. The camera network is isolated

| | |
|---|---|
| **What we do** | From a camera's network segment, attempt to reach the internet, your family devices, and the management interfaces. |
| **What you should see** | All attempts fail. The recorder can still reach the cameras. |
| **Why it matters** | A compromised camera cannot call home, cannot scan your network, and cannot send video anywhere. This is why the manufacturer's own app will not work — that is by design, and we told you during design. |
| Result | ☐ Pass ☐ Fail |
| Notes | |

## 6b. The router cannot be administered from the recorder

| | |
|---|---|
| **What we do** | From the machine that records your cameras, we try to open the router's administration page **at every one of its addresses** — one per network segment. |
| **What you should see** | **All of them fail.** Not the first one: all of them. |
| **Why it matters** | Your router has an interface on every network it serves, and they are all the same administration page. From the recorder, one of those addresses is its own gateway. If only one were blocked, anyone who took control of the recorder could reconfigure the network that is supposed to contain it — open a port, or switch off the camera segment's isolation. |
| Addresses tested | {% for v in vlans_presentes %}`10.{{ red.octeto }}.{{ v.id }}.1` {% endfor %} |
| Result | ☐ Pass ☐ Fail |
| Notes | |

## 7. The support switch, and its expiry

| | |
|---|---|
| **What we do** | You turn on support access from your dashboard. We connect. Then we wait for it to expire, or shorten the timer to demonstrate it. |
| **What you should see** | A notification when the session opens. A countdown on your dashboard. A notification when it closes. Our access stops working the moment it expires. The event is written to a log **on your machine** that you can read. |
| **Also demonstrated** | Restarting the controller during an open session revokes access immediately. |
| **Why it matters** | We hold no standing access to your system. This is the control that guarantees it. |
| Result | ☐ Pass ☐ Fail |
| Log shown to customer | ☐ Yes |

## 8. Backup and restore

| | |
|---|---|
| **What we do** | Run a backup, then restore a configuration file from it and show you the restored content. |
| **What you should see** | The backup completes, is encrypted, and restores correctly. |
| **You are told, and you acknowledge** | **Video is not backed up.** It is protected by drive redundancy only, where your package includes redundancy. **Redundancy is not backup.** The encryption key is yours; we do not keep a copy, and **without it the backup cannot be recovered**. |
| Result | ☐ Pass ☐ Fail |
| Customer acknowledges video is not backed up | ☐ Yes |

